{"path":"utility/initializer_list/initializer_list","title":"std::initializer_list<T>::initializer_list","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::initializer_list&lt;T&gt;::</span>initializer_list","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/initializer_list/initializer_list","section":"utility","kind":"page","summary":"Constructs an empty initializer list.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td><div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">initializer_list<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> </td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx14\">(constexpr since C++14)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Constructs an empty initializer list.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Constant\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Despite a lack of constructors, it is possible to create non-empty initializer lists.  Instances of <code>std::initializer_list</code> are implicitly constructed when:\n</p>\n<ul><li> a <i>braced-init-list</i> is used in <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/list_initialization\">list-initialization</a>, including function-call list initialization and assignment expressions (not to be confused with <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/initializer_list\">constructor initializer lists</a>)\n</li><li> a <i>braced-init-list</i> is bound to <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">auto</span></span>, including in a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/range-for\">ranged for loop</a>\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;initializer_list&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/initializer_list\"><span class=\"kw964\">std::<span class=\"me2\">initializer_list</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> empty_list<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"empty_list.size(): \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> empty_list.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// create initializer lists using list-initialization</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/initializer_list\"><span class=\"kw964\">std::<span class=\"me2\">initializer_list</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> digits<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">4</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">5</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"digits.size(): \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> digits.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// special rule for auto means 'fractions' has the</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// type std::initializer_list&lt;double&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> fractions <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu16\">3.14159</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">2.71828</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"fractions.size(): \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> fractions.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// create constexpr initializer list (since C++14)</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">static</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> ab <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">'a'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'b'</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    static_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span>ab.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span> and <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>ab.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"st0\">'a'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>empty_list.size(): 0\ndigits.size(): 5\nfractions.size(): 2</code></pre> \n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"},{"path":"utility/initializer_list","title":"std::initializer_list"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::initializer_list<T>::initializer_list","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Constructs an empty initializer list."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Constant"},{"label":"Notes","note":"Despite a lack of constructors, it is possible to create non-empty initializer lists."},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++11","C++14"],"wordCount":162,"codeBlockCount":2}
